WEBVTT

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.810
What do you think? Spacious, isn't it?

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.980
There's a lot of storage space too.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.020
Not to mention your own bathroom and toilet.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.900
Is this mirror included as well?

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:35.820
Y-Yes... there's one in every room.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.200
When this building was first built, it was only rented out to women.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.280
If you want, we can remove it.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.330
Nah, it's fine.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:46.460
As you can probably see, I'm picky about how I look.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.590
With regards to rent, this is about as low as I can accept for this place.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:52.840
Seriously?

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.920
Yes, of course. It's because this room is-

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.580
It's just my imagination, right?

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.700
It's cold.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.880
Not again. This is getting annoying...

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.510
H-H-Hot!

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.010
Hot...

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.720
No, I'm okay.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.520
I have my own.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.480
I'm sorry. Hearing your voice out of the blue like that just startled me a little.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.730
Here.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.860
Thanks.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.120
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.500
Is something wrong?

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.210
You've been apologizing this entire time.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.840
I have? I'm sorry.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.420
See? You did it again.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.010
By the way, can I help you with anything?

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.300
I just came to thank you for the other day.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.390
Where's Detective Goto?

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.100
He took yesterday and today off.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:33.400
But it seems like he was around this morning.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.830
I'm home.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.880
I didn't forget.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.070
An exchange diary?

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.820
Why are you laughing at me?

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.450
You're the one who asked if I'd ever dated.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:29.540
Well, I don't think exchange diaries exactly count.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.040
Besides, that was back in middle school, right?

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.080
Actually, that was in high school...

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.420
You had an exchange diary while you were in high school?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.590
I really can't believe you.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:41.170
Just leave me alone.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.880
I suspected that was the case.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:50.600
You really don't care about your appearance, do you?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.430
Hey, that's so rude!

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.600
I <i>do</i> wear make-up and I <i>do</i> dress up.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.020
That's not what I meant.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.440
You don't care what guys think about you, do you?

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.240
If you're going to dress up,

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.160
you need to convince the guys that you're beautiful and cute.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.870
You don't just dress for yourself anymore.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.000
Say, doesn't the world seem like a completely different place once you have a boyfriend?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:20.340
Yup, it's as if you're viewing the world through rose-colored glasses. The entire world is dyed pink.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:25.630
We really want you to experience this happiness too.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.470
Saito Yakumo.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.390
What?

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.390
You were just thinking of him, weren't you?

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.140
D-Don't be silly...

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.270
There's no point in lying.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:41.900
Everyone knows you've been seeing him a lot lately.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.990
He's the psychic that saved my life, right?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.110
Is that how you met him?

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.740
Was I your little cupid?

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.410
How far have you gotten with him?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.250
Well, I'm not really too sure myself.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:06:00.250
He insults me every time I see him, and honestly...

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.630
it really irritates me that he insults me, but I feel that I can be my real self around him.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.840
Strangely enough, I feel really comfortable around him.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.550
So, what you feel towards him is like what you'd feel say, towards an older brother?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.010
That sounds about right.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:15.350
Then, you've never seen him as a man?

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.100
Now that you mention it...

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.730
I do... sort of...

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.110
I think...

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.360
Well, which is it?

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:33.450
Yakumo-kun keeps his emotions locked up inside of him.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:37.870
He keeps all his suffering and sadness to himself.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.130
Watching him like this saddens me,

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:45.420
so I figured that if I could help him in some way-

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.380
What?

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.430
Th-They're gone...

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.400
Yo.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.160
He's sleeping again.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.830
You again.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.670
You didn't have to be <i>that</i> surprised.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.720
Don't you have something better to do than to come here all the time?

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.430
Just how much free time do you have?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.300
I'm a fairly busy person thank you very much.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:38.560
I go to all my classes and I'm busy preparing for an upcoming concert that my club is holding.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.440
I'm completely different from a certain someone who spends all his days sleeping like a cat.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.190
Yet despite all this, you're still getting fatter.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.690
Excuse me?

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.320
You've become noticeably fatter since I met you.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.440
What?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.410
How rude of you!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:56.700
I can't believe this. You're really insensitive!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.710
I don't need someone who just interrupted my nap to lecture me about insensitivity.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.710
You're changing the subject again. You always do that.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.130
Now, that <i>is</i> rude.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.550
The topic keeps jumping around precisely because I'm talking to a scatterbrain like you.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.470
I keep having to steer the conversation back to the topic at hand.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.390
Oh? Is that so?

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:17.970
I'm going home.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:26.480
And? What kind of trouble did you bring with you today?

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.990
He saw right through me...

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.410
I see... A ghost appears in his room.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:40.830
So? What does Date Shota expect me to do?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.250
He wants you to get rid of it.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.670
I'll obviously need to investigate his room,

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.880
but before that, I'd like to talk to his real estate agent.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.130
Why?

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.170
You're as dumb as always.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:52.760
What?

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.760
Why do you think the rent's so low?

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.550
I see!

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:01.270
The landlord knows about it. That's why the rent's so low.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.940
I see, so you're looking for a room, right?

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.650
Will you be living together?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.770
Nope.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.030
Oh, please accept my apologies.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.280
I was so certain that you two were a couple.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.950
That will never happen.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.410
You hate being mistaken as my lover <i>that</i> much?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.540
Actually, I am a psychic.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:24.660
What?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.460
Date Shota-san, a second year at Meisei University.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:32.050
I'm investigating this as per his request.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.760
So, it did...

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:41.140
Our objective is to help people troubled by supernatural phenomena.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.470
We charge-

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.640
Nothing at all.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.560
If that's the case...

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:53.940
To be honest with you, we've had huge problems trying to rent out that room.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.400
Your privacy will be protected

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.570
and we cooperate with legitimate organizations only, so please don't worry.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:05.290
If you like, you can check with a man named Goto Kazutoshi who works for the Seta-machi Police.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.840
Excuse me.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.590
May I ask you a few questions?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.630
Shut up. Get out of my sight.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:21.640
We were notified by residents that there was a suspicious man in the vicinity.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.180
Could you please show me some form of identification?

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:29.850
I'm one of you, idiot.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.860
Shiobara Kimiko-san.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:34.730
Yes.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.360
It's been almost a year now.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.740
I was the first to find her.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.330
The police told us that she died from an illness.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.210
This was also confirmed by her family.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.500
She suffered from some sort of chronic disease in her respiratory system.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:58.090
Ever since then, ghosts have started to appear in that room.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:02.600
I'd like some further information on her.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.010
Let's visit her former workplace.

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:06.600
You know where she worked?

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.480
It says so here.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:16.400
Kimi-chan was a really hardworking girl.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.900
How was her relationships with her coworkers?

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.950
What? That's...

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.450
Don't worry. Please tell me truthfully.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.790
She'll be happier too.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:30.410
Well, since you asked and you're her family...

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.420
I guess I should tell you the truth.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.460
I'm not going to say anything bad about her,

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:41.010
but she could be quite stubborn... well, stubborn might be a little harsh.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.430
I guess she was just too serious.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.850
I see...

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:50.310
Here, this was taken at last year's end-of-the-year party.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:52.190
That's her.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:55.980
I'm not insulting her or anything, but she didn't use make-up,

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:59.030
and she didn't really care about what she wore either.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.700
That's why I tried to give her some advice.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.280
I told her that if she didn't start dressing a little more feminine,

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:07.200
she'd never be able to obtain a woman's true happiness.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.000
May I borrow this photograph?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.660
Of course.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.090
We're almost at Date-san's place.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.310
We'll phone him once we get there and-

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.140
What's wrong?

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:31.730
What?

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.230
You're strangely quiet for once.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.350
I was just thinking.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.230
Haruka-chan!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.240
Are you okay?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.740
I'm perfectly fine.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.660
Hello, it's been a while.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.240
You're Ishii-san, right?

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:50.870
I remember you.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.250
You must be Ozawa Haruka-san, right?

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.380
Yes, I am.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.010
I know this isn't the first time we met,

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.130
but it is the first time <i>we</i> have actually met.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.300
I'm Hijikata Makoto from the Hokuto Press.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.010
Thank you for everything.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:12.520
No, the pleasure was all mine.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.020
I know!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.900
Why don't you join us, Haruka-chan?

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:17.690
What?

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:26.160
Makoto-san invited me out for dinner at her favorite restaurant to celebrate her recovery.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.360
But...

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.040
Geez, Yakumo-kun...

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.910
I'm sorry. I'm in a hurry.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.500
Haruka-chan!

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:46.840
It's rare for you to treat me.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.220
Just shut up and eat.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:54.980
I'll have these enlarged chicken livers, these intestinal membranes, and...

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.900
This must be cows' aorta!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.650
I'll take some of these too.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.360
S-Sure.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.990
So white liver, shiro, and hatsumoto.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.990
I finally found it!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.290
Yakumo-kun, it's me.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.410
You still here?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:40.560
The Film Club's room doesn't have a shower, so I asked Date-san if I could use his.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:43.520
I never asked you about that.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.530
More importantly, why did you leave me behind?

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.530
I never asked you to come with me in the first place.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.570
And there you go saying things like that again...

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:56.700
Geez... You took the map and then you didn't even answer my calls...

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.710
I really had to search for this place.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:08.840
So, this is what a man's room is like...

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:25.570
I'm sorry.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:27.070
What?

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.070
What is it?

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:35.450
Well, I never imagined you as the apologizing type.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:08.780
If I remember correctly, there's a mirror in every room, right?

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:13.110
Yes, that's what Date-san was told when he rented this room.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.030
That's just the real estate agent's excuse.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:19.290
This was installed by a tenant.

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:21.290
How can you tell?

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:26.290
It's too close to the floor and it's crooked.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.340
There's no way a professional would make a mistake like that.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.720
You're right...

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:37.550
Assuming she installed this herself... judging by her height...

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:40.930
the mirror's bracket should be around this height.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:44.310
Then are you saying Kimiko-san installed it herself?

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.860
No, we can't be certain that she did.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.440
Her coworker said that she didn't care about her own appearance.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.200
So why would she need such a large mirror?

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.660
That's...

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.340
I understand.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.050
What are you doing?

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.470
What's this?

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:25.850
Don't open it. Just burn it.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.600
That's her wish.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.870
What's wrong?

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.290
Hey, Nao.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.340
Nao?

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:54.760
Hey!

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.140
It's ready.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.600
Let's begin.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.650
What's wrong?

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:18.200
Hey!

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:22.160
I knew it.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.130
The mirror belonged to her.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:36.550
She didn't want anyone's praise.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.430
She just wanted to be beautiful for herself.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:44.010
That's probably what she thought when she stood in front of that mirror.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:46.930
So why hide this photograph?

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:53.400
Some people are just too shy to wear make-up and dress up in front of others.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:59.950
For Kimiko-san, this was her other self that she didn't want anyone else to know about.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:09.580
Her ghost is here.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.420
Is she mad because I looked at her photograph?

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.960
No, she doesn't appear to be.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.670
I'm sorry I broke our promise.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:22.470
I'm sending this back to you now.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.030
Kimiko-san...

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.090
She's telling you...

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.090
to do your best too.

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:04.260
Yep, I will!

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:13.980
Thank you.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.950
My... other self...

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.760
So, how's it going, Yakumo?

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:48.430
Have you made any more progress with Haruka-chan yet?

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.680
I refuse to answer such ridiculous questions.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.890
I'm completely serious.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:59.270
All humans are loved by another and build up emotions with them.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:04.150
That's nature's providence. There's no way around it.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:08.240
And it's pointless to question it.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:15.790
A bug with wings has no idea why, but it can't help but want to fly.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:21.340
When two people can't help but seek one another out, I think,

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.470
in essence, it's exactly the same scenario.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:31.430
Every human has another personality that they keep hidden from others.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:38.560
I wonder if she has another identity other than being a mother then.

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:48.240
When we get back, I'll tell Date-senpai that it's okay for him to return to his room now.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.870
Nao-chan looks different today, don't you think?

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:54.830
She does?

00:21:55.460 --> 00:22:00.460
The only thing different about her is that she's wearing a new cardigan.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:03.460
Well, come on, if you know, you should tell her.

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:04.050
What?

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:05.550
Don't "what" me.

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:06.970
Geez...

